              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for a prologue, then the Latin for a mime dancer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: imāgō, imāginis",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imāgō, imāginis — \"an image, likeness, portrait\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In ātriō imāginēs maiōrum sunt. In the hall there are portraits of the ancestors."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, third declension. Also the wax masks of ancestors kept in the hall. English image."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "imāgō is usually linked with imitor \"to copy\" (Lewis & Short; EtymDB). English image and imagine come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
